ize\n    return hash_value\n```\n*Note: In practice, languages use optimized hash functions (e.g., MurmurHash, xxHash) and often compute a larger hash code before applying modulo.*\n\n## 2. Collisions\n\nA **collision** occurs when two distinct keys hash to the same index. Since the number of possible keys is usually much larger than the size of the array, collisions are inevitable. There are two primary strategies for handling collisions: **Chaining** and **Open Addressing**.\n\n### 2.1 Chaining\nIn chaining,"
