values) % array_size\n```\n\n## 3. Collisions\n\nA **collision** occurs when two different keys hash to the same index. Since the hash function maps a large (or infinite) set of keys to a finite number of indices, collisions are inevitable. The choice of collision resolution strategy significantly impacts performance.\n\n### Collision Resolution Strategies\n\n#### A. Separate Chaining\nIn separate chaining, each bucket contains a linked list (or another dynamic structure) of entries that hash to that index. When a collision occurs, the new entry is simply added to the list at that bucket.\n\n**Advantages**:\n-"
